<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended October 9, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Oct 9   Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.34   +0.138    +0.303</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     3.96   -0.892    -6.557</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.51   -1.387    +4.928</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 150.90   -1.300   -15.700</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  29.88   -0.068    +0.665</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			    Aug	  July</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-11.12	-12.63</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     640.31	639.55</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.94	107.83</p>
<p>					  Aug 96    July 96	Aug 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.47	63.02	57.73</p>
<p>M2					389.10     389.79     380.70</p>
<p>M3					482.44     482.13     462.46</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
